"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[61138],{261138:e=>{e.exports="# Building a Dashboard Page\n\nElements to include when dispatching the dashboard-authoring sub-agent to construct or modify a dashboard page. Use only the elements that apply to the call.\n\n## Elements\n\n- **Page identification.** `displayName` and `refName` (e.g., `pages/sales_overview`). When creating, include the intended ordering.\n- **Functional context.** 2-3 sentences on what the dashboard is for and what this page conveys to its audience. Derive from the workbook's worksheet titles, dashboard captions, and the parameter/filter set.\n- **Datasets.** Metric views to register on the dashboard for this page (idempotent — skip if already registered): `<metric_view_name> — <displayName>`.\n- **Widgets.** For each: title, chart type, dataset, layout, encodings (use `MEASURE(<name>)` for measures), optional filters/sort/options.\n- **Page filters.** Filter widgets scoped to this page (not widget-scoped): field, widget type, layout, and the `applies-to` widget list. See `filters.md` for the page-vs-widget-vs-global routing.\n\nFor a focused-fix dispatch, include only the elements that change — typically a single widget or a single filter — plus a one-line description of the mismatch and the required change.\n\n## Template\n\nUse this for the prompt body of a per-page call. Omit any line for an element that doesn't apply.\n\n```\nCreate dashboard page \"<page_displayName>\" (refName: <pages/...>; ordering: <0-based index>).\n\nFunctional context: <2-3 sentences on what this page conveys to its audience>.\n\nDatasets to register on the dashboard for this page (idempotent — skip if already registered):\n- <metric_view_name_1> — <displayName>\n- <metric_view_name_2> — <displayName>\n\nWidgets:\n\n1. <widget_title>\n   chartType: <bar|line|area|pie|scatter|counter|...>\n   dataset: <dataset_name>\n   layout: { row: <r>, column: <c>, width: <w>, height: <h> }   # 12-col grid; counters: height ≤ 2\n   encodings:\n     x: { field: <dimension_name>, scale: <categorical|temporal|quantitative> }\n     y: { field: MEASURE(<measure_name>), scale: quantitative }\n     color: { field: <dimension_name>, scale: categorical }\n   filters:\n     - <field> <op> <value>\n   sort:\n     - field: <field>; direction: <asc|desc>\n   options:\n     showDataLabels: <true|false>\n     legend: <true|false>\n\n2. <next widget>\n...\n\nPage filters (separate from widget-scoped filters; see filters.md for page-vs-widget-vs-global routing):\n- field: <field>; widget type: <dropdown|multi-select|date-range|...>; layout: { row, column, width, height }; applies to widgets: [<widget_titles>]\n```\n\n## Field Reference Conventions\n\n- **Dimensions** — backtick the field name only when it contains spaces or special characters.\n- **Measures** — always `MEASURE(<name>)`. The sub-agent translates this into the widget's expression form.\n- **Field names** must match the metric-view dimension/measure names exactly — case-sensitive.\n\n## Layout Constraints\n\n- 12-column grid: `column + width ≤ 12`, `width ≥ 1`, `height ≥ 1`.\n- Counter / KPI widgets: `height ≤ 2`.\n- Filter widgets: typically `height = 1`.\n\n## What NOT to Include\n\n- The source Tableau workbook content — the sub-agent doesn't need it and it bloats the call.\n- A reused prompt copied across pages by find-and-replace — every dispatch must reflect that page's specific filters, layout, and functional context.\n- Page filters without an `applies-to` list — without it the filter widget appears but does nothing.\n"}}]);
